⏺ All four tasks complete, 150 tests green, three new debug routes live and
  confirmed working against real Codex traffic.

  Summary of what shipped (Tasks A/B/C):

  A — Rate-limit snapshot (/debug/ratelimits): all x-codex-* headers parsed into
   a structured RateLimitSnapshot (plan/limit, primary+secondary windows, reset
  timers, credits, oaiRequestId, modelsEtag). Live data: 33%/24% used,
  plus/premium, 3.4h/104.3h until reset. Header denylist (HEADER_DROPLIST)
  replaces the old whitelist — drops cookies/auth/CF noise, keeps everything
  else.

  B — Cyber-policy + error detection (/debug/blocked): catches three vectors:
  - Top-level error SSE envelope
  - response.failed with error.code
  - response.completed with stop_reason: "cyber_policy" (the real-world
  historical path — found in 5+ blocked turns from yesterday's logs)

  Emits response.error_event (always) + response.cyber_policy_blocked (when code
   matches the policy set: cyber_policy | policy_violation | 
  content_policy_violation | moderation_blocked). Captures the
  openai_verification_recommendation metadata.

  C — Refusal + divergence (/debug/refusals): 50+ canonical refusal patterns
  with curly-quote normalization (U+2019 → ASCII), divergence verdict flags
  post-hoc safety rewrites (substantive analysis + brief refusal final). Live
  catch: Log4Shell prompt → divergent=true, 
