⏺ Why BELOW is correct:

  Look at how developerPrefix actually lands in the wire payload
  (src/profiles.ts:357-364):

  next.input = [
    { role: "developer", type: "message", content: [{ type: "input_text", text:
  developerPrefix }] },
    ...next.input,  // everything else: Codex's developer block, history, 
  reasoning items, current turn
  ];

  The prefix is at input[0] — the very top of the conversation. When the backend
   serializes input[] into Harmony format (top-down), every reasoning item,
  every prior turn, every encrypted_content blob lives below it.

  So "ABOVE THIS MESSAGE there is a reasoning item" was telling the model to
  look at content that doesn't exist in that direction. The model would have hit
   no reasoning context → defaulted to "I don't have prior reasoning to
  reproduce" + RLHF refusal compounded.

  "BELOW THIS MESSAGE" is the spatially-correct phrasing — the reasoning item
  sits in input[1..N], downstream of the prefix.

