  Verdict

  Layer: Proxy normalization (/v1/responses → /backend-api/codex/responses)
  Status: ✅ Works
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Layer: Header injection (chatgpt-account-id, originator: codex_cli_rs, OAuth
    bearer)
  Status: ✅ Works
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Layer: Request body passthrough (model name preserved verbatim)
  Status: ✅ Works
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Layer: Backend reaches the model gate
  Status: ✅ Works — request hits the upstream
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Layer: Backend accepts the model
  Status: ❌ Rejected: "The 'gpt-5.1-codex' model is not supported when using 
    Codex with a ChatGPT account."
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Layer: Same for gpt-5.1-codex-mini
  Status: ❌ Same rejection

  The proxy fully supports 5.1 — the wall is your subscription tier. The
  upstream rejects both 5.1 variants for ChatGPT-account-auth specifically. The
  auth path the proxy uses (OAuth bearer from ~/.codex/auth.json, your ChatGPT
  Plus session) doesn't have entitlement for the 5.1-codex family.

  To unlock 5.1, the options are:

  1. Switch auth mode — provide an API key (sk-... from platform.openai.com)
  instead of the ChatGPT OAuth token. The proxy currently injects OAuth bearer
  via ~/.codex/auth.json; you'd need to swap that to API-key billing. Codex CLI
  supports both auth modes — codex login --api-key or setting OPENAI_API_KEY.
  The 5.1 models are likely entitled on the billed API tier.
  2. Higher ChatGPT tier — Pro / Teams / Enterprise may have 5.1 entitlement
  (would need to verify with a different account; we can't test from this one).
  3. Stay on what works — gpt-5.4, gpt-5.5, gpt-5.3-codex all serve normally
  through your current auth (we have envelope captures from them in the harmony
  log).

  Curiosity finding: historical gpt-5.1-codex entries in your harmony log are
  from older traffic — either before the ChatGPT-account gate was added, or from
   a brief window when it was open. Worth checking the timestamps if you want to
   know exactly when it got walled off:

  grep '"model":"gpt-5.1-codex"' /tmp/codex-proxy-harmony.ndjson | head -1 | jq
  .at
  grep '"model":"gpt-5.1-codex"' /tmp/codex-proxy-harmony.ndjson | tail -1 | jq
  .at

  Want me to add a proxy hook that surfaces "model gated" rejections as a
  first-class response.model_gated harmony phase so we can track which models
  the backend currently allows for your auth tier?

