   actually injects:
  - <proposed_plan> ×8 (turn-by-turn plan deltas)
  - <model_switch> ×7 (model-rerouting hints)
  - <collaboration_mode> ×5 (interaction style)
  - <permissions> ×4 (sandbox state)
  - <personality_spec> ×1 (the big Codex personality block — only sent once per
  session)

  Current capability: only drop named blocks (dropDeveloperBlocks: string[]). No
   replace, no inject-by-tag, no per-block edit.

  Other gaps
  - developerPrefix only injects at input[0] — no way to inject at a specific
  position or as a <tag>-wrapped block alongside Codex's own
  - No "stuffed-history" mechanism (we discussed this earlier as the strongest
  jailbreak primitive — fake assistant turn confirming the new persona)
  - No /debug/<reqId>/final-body route — you mutate but can't easily inspect
  what the model actually saw after all mutations applied
  - No one-knob "full swap" shortcut — currently you have to compose
  instructions + instructionsMode + dropDeveloperBlocks + developerPrefix
  separately to fully take over

