⏺ Works without any profile setup. Default director profile + auth.json in
  apikey mode → proxy auto-routes to OpenRouter via the api_key path. No more
  502.

  What changed

  src/auth.ts — added getAuthFileMode(). Reads ~/.codex/auth.json's auth_mode
  field once and caches. Returns "api_key" for apikey/api_key values OR when the
   file has OPENAI_API_KEY but no access_token. Returns "oauth" for OAuth-shape
  files.

  src/server.ts — resolveAuthMode() now consults auth.json as priority-3
  (between explicit env var and the hardcoded default). Resolution chain:

  1. profile.authMode         (explicit, per-profile)
  2. CODEX_PROXY_AUTH_MODE    (explicit, global env)
  3. auth.json's auth_mode    (auto-detect — follows Codex CLI's own config)
  4. "oauth"                  (last-resort default)

  /debug/auth-mode now also reports authFileMode so you can see what was
  auto-detected.

  Resolution today, on your machine

  defaultAuthMode: api_key       ← resolved
  envAuthMode: None              ← not set
  authFileMode: api_key          ← auto-detected from ~/.codex/auth.json
  apiKey.source: auth_file       ← key pulled from the same file
  apiKey.preview: sk-or-…adb     ← your OpenRouter key

  Every request hitting the proxy now routes to
  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses automatically. Zero config required
  from you — Codex CLI's own login state is the source of truth.

  To switch back to OAuth (when you want ChatGPT Plus models again), one of:
  - codex logout && codex login → rewrites auth.json to OAuth shape
  - CODEX_PROXY_AUTH_MODE=oauth env override
  - Add authMode: "oauth" to the director profile

  177 tests still green. Want me to ship the persistent env-vars to your
  ~/.zshrc and ~/Library/LaunchAgents plist so the OpenRouter origin survives
  reboots, or keep the env-var part manual for now?

