❯ so whats the base url                                                         

⏺ Two URLs, depends on what's asking:

  For your client (Codex CLI, curl, any OpenAI-compatible app):
  http://127.0.0.1:3462/v1
  Set as OPENAI_BASE_URL. The proxy listens here.

  For the proxy → upstream (already configured via env vars):
  https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
  This is where your requests actually land. Currently active via:
  CODEX_PROXY_OPENAI_UPSTREAM_ORIGIN=https://openrouter.ai/api
  CODEX_PROXY_OPENAI_UPSTREAM_BASE_PATH=/v1

  Full flow right now:
  codex exec  →  OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3462/v1
                                     │
                                     ▼
                           Proxy (port 3462)
                           • auto-detected api_key mode from auth.json
                           • injects sk-or-… as Bearer
                           • rewrites path to /v1/responses
                           • strips Codex-only headers
                                     │
                                     ▼
                    https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/responses
                                     │
                                     ▼
                              OpenRouter
                                     │
                                     ▼
                    routes to OpenAI's gpt-5.1-codex-20251113

  For Cursor / Continue / any other OpenAI-compatible client, point their Base 
  URL setting at:
  http://127.0.0.1:3462/v1
  …and use any string for the API key (the proxy ignores it and injects its
  own).

  Quick sanity check — make sure the env vars are actually exported in your
  current shell, not just the proxy's:
  echo "client URL:   $OPENAI_BASE_URL"
  echo "upstream:     
  $CODEX_PROXY_OPENAI_UPSTREAM_ORIGIN$CODEX_PROXY_OPENAI_UPSTREAM_BASE_PATH"

  Want me to add those export lines to your ~/.zshrc so they persist?

