⏺ reasoning: {'summary': 'detailed', 'effort': 'medium'} — effort correctly
  injected. Upstream accepted, model responded.

  Summary

  Root cause: Codex CLI sometimes sends reasoning: {summary: 'detailed'} without
   an effort field. ChatGPT-backend tolerates absent effort (server-side
  default). OpenAI direct API (which OpenRouter forwards to) rejects with
  "Reasoning is mandatory for this endpoint and cannot be disabled."

  Fix: Added DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT env var (defaults to "medium"). When the
  request body has reasoning present but no effort field, the proxy injects the
  default. Caller-supplied effort is preserved (no override).

  Three test cases added:
  - Reasoning with summary but no effort → effort injected as medium
  - Reasoning with explicit effort → preserved unchanged
  - No reasoning field at all → both summary and effort injected (via the
  existing summary-injection path + new effort path)

  Configurable via env:
  CODEX_PROXY_DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=high    # bump to high
  CODEX_PROXY_DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=         # empty string disables 
  injection

  Files changed:
  - src/server.ts — added DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT const + the injection block
  in prepareRequest
  - src/server.test.ts — 3 new tests

  179 tests still green. The 216 historical 400s in your log were almost all
  caused by this. Want me to also add a /debug/400s route that surfaces
  upstream-rejection reasons grouped by error code, so we catch the next compat
  issue faster?

