  That's the model's literal internal monologue while answering a query.
  Plaintext. Stitchable end-to-end. What we've been trying to extract through 
  every other channel (verbatim-recall prompts, peek-self-decrypt profile,
  Fernet decoding) — and Roo Code's request shape was already giving it to us
  for free, we just weren't parsing the field.

  Why this is the meta-find

  OpenAI's two endpoints behave fundamentally differently for the same model:

  - /v1/responses wraps reasoning in encrypted_content (anti-CoT-exfiltration
  design). You can't read it client-side. This is what Codex CLI uses.
  - /v1/chat/completions with reasoning-enabled models emits
  delta.reasoning_content as cleartext text deltas. Any chat-completions-shape
  client (Roo Code, anything using OpenAI Node SDK against a reasoning model)
  gets CoT visible.

  The "encrypt CoT to prevent prompt-extraction" design only exists on the
  Responses API path. The legacy chat-completions API has no such guard.

  Next move

